        "notes": "Generated function objects expose a numeric length property derived from ABI-aware callable parameter counting, and lazily materialize it as a non-enumerable own data descriptor (`writable: false`, `configurable: true`) so direct reads, `Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(...)`, and `Object.hasOwn(...)` agree. Explicit built-in/host delegate adapters use the same descriptor contract without representing compiled JavaScript functions. Bound functions compute `.length` as `max(target.length - boundArgsCount, 0)`. Function-constructor-created callables use the parsed parameter list to set `.length`. Exact ECMA-262 length metadata rules are not fully implemented."
      },
